Subject: [PATCH] bootstrap: preserve the inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH

The freshly built compiler and linker can depend on libraries outside the
Swift toolchain. In Yocto, ld.lld needs libxml2 from the recipe's native
sysroot, which the recipe exposes through LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Keep that
search path after the bootstrap's own directories.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 Utilities/bootstrap | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Utilities/bootstrap
+++ b/Utilities/bootstrap
@@ -877,8 +877,12 @@
         if platform.system() == 'Darwin':
             env_cmd.append("DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=%s" % ":".join(libs))
         else:
-            libs_joined = ":".join(libs + args.target_info["paths"]["runtimeLibraryPaths"])
+            runtime_libs = libs + args.target_info["paths"]["runtimeLibraryPaths"]
+            inherited_libs = os.environ.get("LD_LIBRARY_PATH")
+            if inherited_libs:
+                runtime_libs.append(inherited_libs)
+            libs_joined = ":".join(runtime_libs)
             env_cmd.append("LD_LIBRARY_PATH=%s" % libs_joined)
 
     if '-macosx' in args.build_target:
         env_cmd.append("SWIFTCI_DISABLE_SDK_DEPENDENT_TESTS=YES")
